-- workflows.flow
-- Orchestration. A workflow runs inline with the request that started it, and
-- USING binds an argument from an earlier step's output.
--
-- Modifier order: USING must come first; RETRY and TIMEOUT may follow in either
-- order. TIMEOUT is a real deadline enforced with AbortController -- the backend
-- request is genuinely cancelled -- and it applies per attempt, not per step.

-- The booking happy path.
--
-- charge_booking and reserve_inventory are independent of each other and both
-- depend only on create_booking, so they run concurrently.
--
-- PARALLEL takes only STEPs: at least two, no duplicate action inside one block,
-- and no CONFIRM. That last restriction is load-bearing. A confirmation pauses
-- the workflow and a pause writes exactly one record keyed by one token; two
-- members pausing would need two, and members that already finished have
-- committed side effects that cannot be replayed.
--
-- A member may not bind from a sibling either -- members are dispatched
-- together, so a sibling's output does not exist yet at dispatch time.
WORKFLOW BookingCheckout

  STEP create_booking

  PARALLEL
    STEP charge_booking    USING booking_id = create_booking.id RETRY 3 TIMEOUT 5000
    STEP reserve_inventory USING booking_id = create_booking.id TIMEOUT 3000
  END

  STEP send_confirmation USING booking_id = create_booking.id RETRY 2

END

-- Cancellation, branching on whether the booking was already paid for.
--
-- cancel_booking is CONFIRM-gated, so this workflow pauses at that step and
-- emits workflow.paused. The caller completes it through POST /workflows/resume,
-- and the step's RETRY and TIMEOUT are carried through the resume rather than
-- being dropped.
WORKFLOW BookingCancellation

  STEP cancel_booking

  IF cancel_booking.total_cents
    STEP refund_booking USING booking_id = cancel_booking.id RETRY 3 TIMEOUT 8000
  ELSE
    STEP send_confirmation USING booking_id = cancel_booking.id
  END

END

-- Multi-way dispatch on a value returned by the backend.
--
-- SWITCH compares stringified, so CASE 2 matches a numeric 2 arriving as JSON.
-- No match and no DEFAULT is a runtime error rather than silent fall-through --
-- "possibly nothing" is spelled DEFAULT with an empty body.
WORKFLOW PostStayFollowUp

  STEP create_booking

  SWITCH create_booking.status
    CASE "completed"
      STEP send_confirmation USING booking_id = create_booking.id
    CASE "cancelled"
      STEP refund_booking USING booking_id = create_booking.id
    DEFAULT
      WAIT 1000
  END

END
